    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0215" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v26/pg187"/>

                <head>86. Letter From President Eisenhower to Chancellor Adenauer<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d86-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                        1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Chancellor</hi>: Thank you for your letter
                    of December 4<anchor n="2" xml:id="d86-f2"/> and for the kind sentiments which
                    you expressed in it.</p>
                <p>I agree with you that the major objective of the Soviet Union is to control all
                    of Europe. I think that Americans generally believe, as I do, that the freedom
                    of our own country is bound to the maintenance of the freedom of Europe. The
                    events which have taken place in other parts of the world recently in no way
                    affect our fundamental relationship of interdependence.</p>
                <p>With kindest personal regards,</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dwight D. Eisenhower</hi></signed><anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d86-f3"/></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d86-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d86-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.62A/12–1256. Secret; Presidential
                    Handling. Transmitted to Bonn in telegram 1624, December 12, which is the source
                    text, with the instructions that it be delivered to Adenauer as soon as
                    possible.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d86-f2" n="2" xml:id="d86-f2-content">
